From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Paslawski <chris@paslawski.me>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 22:45:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] sepolicy: allow hardware Codec2 to access app memfd buffers

Origin: Local ThinkSmart View port
Source: https://github.com/LineageOS/android_device_mainline_common
License: Apache-2.0 (modified upstream sources)
Base-commit: f49f55117276cc2603fd7f6aeb78b859535f8e8d

The AIDL Codec2 buffer pool passes app-owned memfd-backed message queues
to the hardware codec service. The dedicated memfd_file class requires
its own permissions; existing file permissions do not cover it.

Without these permissions, Binder rejects the queue's file descriptors
and Codec2 cannot submit compressed input, even after the V4L2 decoder
has started successfully. SmartTube repeatedly fails queueCSDInputBuffer
with C2_CORRUPTED while SELinux denies mediacodec read/write access to the
app's memfd:MessageQueue.

Give the hardware codec domain the same app memfd permissions already
granted to mediaswcodec by the platform policy. Keep access limited to
shared-memory data; do not grant ordinary app-file access.

--- a/sepolicy/vendor/mediacodec.te
+++ b/sepolicy/vendor/mediacodec.te
@@ -1,3 +1,5 @@
 allow mediacodec device:dir r_dir_perms;
 
+allow mediacodec appdomain:memfd_file { getattr read write map };
+
 gpu_access(mediacodec)
